  "observations": [
    "Compared with original, the native cap/visor, rounded head/hair/moustache and folded collar/cuffs/apron form a more coherent warm cartoon. Skin, ginger hair, turquoise cap, ivory coat, green apron, teal tie and dark shoes remain distinct. Broad soft highlights reveal volume in front, profiles and rear without a directional ground shadow or dead dark material patches.",
    "The known N defect is removed in every hold/load frame: the nape remains a natural clean skin/hair contour, without the white plate line/crescent or false smile. No intermittent return appears in the full motion or game-context assemblies.",
    "E/S/W retain complete readable salmon/rice/plate composition through all hold/load phases, including the out-and-back load midpoint and return. They no longer show the round02 profile chin fragment/buried salmon. Logical-size light/gray/dark views and game assemblies retain clear food identity and stable alpha edges.",
    "The native body/knife/rig/action/contact/camera/light/material contract passes, and the exact canonical food remains an honestly identified packed2D billboard. The saved XYZ driver law is one continuous function of ground-root yaw, algebraically equal to the required semantic forward/camera dot law for this fixed camera; no state/frame/facing-name inputs, lookup, hiding, body patch or raster fitting is present.",
    "The polynomial generator0+1*x is a saved native identity mapping on the allowed location-driver fields. It removes old keyed identity snapping of tiny inputs and implements the permitted exact C1 law. Original yaw driver and all other drivers/actions remain exact. This field delta is within v4; it is not per-view fitting."
  ],
  "blockers": [],
  "remainingDifferences": [
    "Compared with the painted target, cloth/hair surfaces have simpler native material texture and the face remains more compact. At logical size these remain coherent, crafted and readable; the frozen aesthetic bar does not require painted microtexture.",
    "Final held/load pixels are not all bit-identical to prior rounds. S24/24 equal01; N22/24 equal02 with two one-pixel one-channel one-level differences and no alpha change. E/W are quantified native output differences, mostly one-level channels, maximum raw8; logical light/gray/dark composite maxima are3 for E and2 for W. Enlarged true composites and full playback show no material silhouette, edge, palette, food-visibility or motion defect. The evidence does not justify calling these random or declaring all food/held pixels identical.",
    "The fresh own closed-copy replay has9/10 exact RGBA frames. Work-N05 has a single G89 versus submittedG90 at native(263,310), unchanged alpha; this one-level difference is visually immaterial and its exact numeric origin was not isolated. The separately submitted closed replay20/20 frames were independently decoded and verified exact.",
    "At nonshipping debug orientations just beyond profile (for example ±90.01degrees), actual old keyed-driver mapping versus the new polynomial can differ by up to0.02197266 export pixel because the old mapping snapped tiny inputs. The new offset satisfies the frozen world-ray law; all192 required shipping evaluations remain below the explicit0.001pixel projection gate. No arbitrary-angle bit-identity claim is made."
  ],
